    "q-107260": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107260",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the volume of the cube whose sides each have length $7\\,\\text{cm}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=7\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV=(7\\,\\text{cm})^{3}=343\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$",
