      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224461/assets/b974b6e782801fbe2099971afd0df9a5c6e05a10afc2ce0e4054c850088e753b.png)\n\nWhat is the volume of the cube?",
      "worked_solution": "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=2\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV=(2\\,\\text{cm})^{3}=8\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{3}.\n$$",
