      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224461/assets/692f2ca65354bd1563ef8a08658644c2cb1793e7c1dfa5e415b63ec95e91b114.png)\n\nWhat is the volume of the cube?",
      "worked_solution": "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=5\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV=(5\\,\\text{m})^{3}=125\\,{\\text{ m}}^{3}.\n$$",
