      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224461/assets/ceaf4ee652448eecc115fbe7f53a3ad2ac9bf255ece8c04674fe2d8d7d6fb324.png)\n\nThe volume of the cube above is $512\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.$ What is the length of its sides?",
      "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{512}=8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $8\\,\\text{in}.$",
