      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224461/assets/ec35ecf376e5f5108d379ee965b8ea7ce32223050fa09e8d90ad2cf769853894.png)\n\nThe volume of the cube above is $1\\,728\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$ What is the length of its sides?",
      "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{1\\,728}=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $12\\,\\text{cm}.$",
